id: pm-csv-71zg
title: Capture prior field values in the transaction record so a failed update can be truly compensated
description: "The atomic import compensates creates by closing them, which is a real inverse: the item did not exist before, so closing it restores the prior state. An update has no inverse without the prior field values, and this extension does not capture them, so the atomic path deliberately skips update compensation. Writing some other value over a failed update would not be a rollback; it would be a second unreviewed mutation on top of a failed one, which on a partially applied import is a worse outcome than a loud identified failure. Making update compensation sound requires capturing the prior field values into the transaction record before each update and compensating from that record. That changes the transaction record format, so it is a real capability with real cost rather than part of a buffer overrun fix. Raised by a Greptile review of PR 59, where the narrower guarantee that no mutation is left un-identified was accepted as the honest ceiling for that PR."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: atomic,csv,rollback,transaction
created_at: "2026-08-09T00:13:19.589Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T08:26:11.464Z"
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "The transaction record stores the prior values of every field an update will modify, written before the update subprocess runs; compensation restores those values rather than writing an invented value; the record format change is versioned so an in-flight transaction written by an older version is detected and refused rather than mis-restored; a regression test drives a mid-import failure after an update and asserts the pre-import field values are restored exactly"
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:41:37.431Z",codex-sol,"Built-package baseline in a scratch pm project: a keyed row changed Original (priority 1) to Changed (priority 3), then a new row with priority 99 failed. After coordinator compensation the original item still had Changed/3. Acceptance: capture a versioned full prior document and immutable history boundary before each update; restore exact absent/empty and collection state under the item lock, refuse intervening non-transaction history, and resume interrupted forward/compensation phases idempotently. Existing item references and pm-csv-5si5 evidence were read; no linked docs, files, or blocking dependencies were listed."
  "2026-10-07T21:48:53.248Z",codex-sol,"Initial real-tracker suite passed 19/19 scenarios: exact prior-state recovery, all coordinator transitions, journal/mutation gaps, duplicate existing keys, legacy plan refusal, record validation, and concurrent subprocess writer refusal. Added immutable update/close inspection for the terminal subprocess gap and a real SIGKILL restart test. The SDK bulk restore helper lacks a concurrent-writer guard, so compensation uses its public mutateItem primitive with the guard inside the item lock. No SDK issue was filed."
  "2026-10-07T21:57:55.152Z",codex-sol,"Exact stored-value checks exposed SDK normalization: empty assignee strings and empty dependency arrays become absent in canonical reads/writes. The record now saves both canonical prior state and original representation/format. Compensation restores canonical state through mutateItem, then uses SDK item lock, atomic file write, and append-only history primitives to preserve original physical fields at the same verified canonical hash. Its final completion receipt follows that write. Seven focused built-package, empty-representation, phase-crash, and writer-gap scenarios passed; a real SIGKILL between update and close also passed. No SDK issue was filed."
  "2026-10-07T22:04:45.050Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: an isolated copy retained the same index, tests and SDK, built successfully, and replaced only compensateUpdate's body with its previous no-op behavior. All three selected tests failed on behavioral assertions (two built-package exact-state cases retained Changed/priority 3/type Feature/lifecycle changes; the independent-writer case lacked the required refusal). The current implementation passed the focused exact-state and writer checks. Existing subprocess fixtures were given a local CommonJS package boundary so an ancestor ESM setting cannot prevent their failure injections from loading."
  "2026-10-07T22:25:21.524Z",codex-sol,"The PM-linked suite passed 32/32 real-tracker scenarios. A further red regression showed restart could lose the update target after another writer replaced all CSV tags. Versioned step identities now bind operation, target id, and row; replay recovers those immutable bindings from the SDK journal. The removed-tags scenario, legacy refusal, keyed resume, rollback retry, and closed-row resume passed 5/5 focused checks. npm/Bun/current and npm/minimum packed acceptance also passed. SDK gaps handled locally: canonical normalization of empty fields and bulk restore without a concurrent-writer guard."
  "2026-10-07T22:29:06.062Z",codex-sol,"Final behavioral revert proof uses identical tests and importer with only compensateUpdate restored to its former no-op behavior. The isolated package compiles, and all four selected tests fail on assertions: unset and empty built-package prior-state restoration, independent body writer refusal, and tag-removal writer refusal. No load failure counts as evidence. Durable step identities now bind the original create/update role and update item id; README and design documentation explain replay after mutable tags disappear. The linked tag-removal test passed through pm test on the current implementation."
  "2026-10-07T22:29:28.976Z",codex-sol,"The full release suite passed all 271 tests with 100% branches and functions. The first line report saw two extra comment lines appended while its source module was already loaded, so that in-flight run failed the unchanged 100% line threshold. Source will now remain frozen for npm and Bun release verification on the committed revision; this failed gate is not approval. Packed acceptance passed npm current, Bun current, and npm minimum peer scenarios. SDK gaps handled locally: canonical empty-value normalization and bulk restore lacking an intervening-writer guard. No SDK issue was filed."
  "2026-10-07T22:40:40.335Z",codex-sol,"The committed npm release gate passed completely: 271 tests and 100% configured line/branch/function coverage, zero production vulnerabilities, and all three packed scenarios. Bun passed all 271 assertions but exposed nondeterministic coverage of the existing silent create-error fallback (99.88% branches). Added a transparent wrapper that delegates the real invalid create and suppresses only its stderr; the scenario must still restore the preceding update exactly and report pm create failed. Thresholds are unchanged. Both release gates will rerun on the final revision."
  "2026-10-07T22:42:47.508Z",codex-sol,"The silent real-create failure regression passed directly and via its PM-linked command. Lint, duplicate and docstring checks passed. Refreshed final behavioral revert: the isolated package compiles cleanly with identical importer/tests and only the compensation body replaced by its former no-op; all four selected tests fail on assertions. The implementation and journal design are unchanged. Final npm and Bun release verification will use the new frozen head, with the extra deterministic failure scenario included."
  "2026-10-11T06:06:03.730Z",codex-sol-review-150,"PR #150 review fixes exclusively owned by codex-sol-review-150 in the detached review worktree. The concurrent toolchain worker must not edit this worktree or reply to PR #150. Verified both inline findings and the README runtime-dependency claim. Plan: discover SDK journals through public dry-run inventory, narrow unknown JSON before using identities, preserve original target/create bindings and SDK validation, add real-journal no-mutation and Git discovery regressions, prove behavioral reverts, then run unchanged full npm/Bun and isolated-identity gates. No nested agents, upstream issues, merge or release."
  "2026-10-11T06:08:57.843Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Journal discovery now uses the existing static SDK import surface and public runWorkspaceTransactionGc with dryRun true and infinite retention. The minimum advertised SDK tarball exports the API with entries.file. Parsed journal data is unknown and narrowed for null, primitive, array, missing stepIds, non-array stepIds and mixed/non-string entries before any mutation. SDK schema/lifecycle validation remains unchanged. Regression fixtures use the real coordinator and journals; no SDK mocks. The Git fixture starts with genuinely untracked synthetic files and checks both ignore decisions and discovery. README now matches the runtime dependency manifest."
  "2026-10-11T06:10:15.236Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Behavioral revert proof: restoring only loadAtomicBindings to its previous behavior and rebuilding makes the malformed SDK journal test fail (1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail, exit 1): null produces Failed to import: Cannot read properties of null (reading stepIds), rather than incompatible CSV step identity. Removing only the parent-directory unignore makes the Git discovery test fail (1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail, exit 1): check-ignore returns 0 instead of expected 1 for the untracked evaluation file. Both fixes restored; initial focused suite passed 3/3. Real minimum SDK 2026.8.20 runtime probe prepared a journal, discovered entries.file, and confirmed old terminal journal bytes unchanged under dry-run infinite retention. No SDK layout relocation is simulated; future layout compatibility follows the public inventory path contract."
  "2026-10-11T06:18:13.624Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator independently verified 2/2 selected review regressions: malformed journal identities refuse with every tracker byte unchanged, and evaluation query fixtures are discoverable while runtime search contents remain ignored. Reviewed the new public SDK dry-run inventory path and shape narrowing; no additional inline SDK loader or mock tracker was introduced."
  "2026-10-11T06:27:16.967Z",codex-agent,Orchestrator review also found the development section repeated the zero-runtime-dependencies claim. Corrected that second occurrence to name the actual @toon-format/toon dependency; the introductory occurrence was already fixed by the review worker. Include both README corrections in the existing outside-diff finding response.
  "2026-10-11T06:37:35.607Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Full npm run release:check passed: 275/275 tests, zero failures, skips or cancellations; configured coverage 100% lines/branches/functions across index.ts, atomic-update.ts and scripts/docstring-gate.ts. All 80 gated declarations documented, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities. Packed npm-current and native bun-current on SDK 2026.10.4 plus npm-minimum on 2026.8.20 passed, as did changelog, release workflow, publish attestation and version-date checks. Final review tests were rerun through pm test with progress after adding both source and built shape cases. Final function-only and ignore-rule-only behavioral reverts each failed exactly one selected test with exit 1, then fixes were restored. The reported child coverage issue did not reproduce, and the existing CommonJS fixture boundary is already explicit; no fixture isolation or toolchain changes were needed."
  "2026-10-11T07:10:06.509Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Full bun run release:check passed with unchanged gates: 275/275 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 100% lines/branches/functions over the same three configured sources. All 80 gated declarations documented, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, all three packed consumer scenarios, changelog consistency, release workflow, publish attestation and version-date checks passed. npm and Bun produced the same package tarball checksum. Tracker commands use CLI 2026.10.11; development SDK gates remain pinned at 2026.10.4, and the real public inventory probe passed on minimum SDK 2026.8.20. Starting the requested isolated-identity full npm gate with temporary HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. No source or threshold changes since the review fixes."
  "2026-10-11T07:37:57.845Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Final local receipts: npm run release:check, bun run release:check, and npm run release:check with managed temporary HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 all exited 0. Each ran 275/275 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations and 100% lines/branches/functions across exactly index.ts, atomic-update.ts and scripts/docstring-gate.ts; all 80 declarations, duplication, production audit, packed consumer matrix, changelog, workflow, attestation and version-date gates passed. Final PM-linked review tests passed 3/3. Reverting only the journal reader and rebuilding fails exactly one malformed-journal test; removing only the directory unignore fails exactly one Git discovery test, each exit 1 with fixes restored. Both README runtime-dependency statements are now accurate. Real minimum SDK inventory availability and unchanged journal bytes were verified; future SDK directory relocation is not mocked. No child coverage failure reproduced in these three gates. A shell-cleanup guard rejection was handled with managed temporary-directory cleanup. After TypeScript and README duplicate searches, recorded the separate compiler-documentation mismatch as open follow-up pm-csv-bqyu for the toolchain workstream. No new upstream issue filed. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; PR #150 remains exclusively this review worker's handoff, with exact-head CI receipts to be added only to the PR after freezing tracked files."
  "2026-10-11T07:41:26.568Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Post-gate tracker checks: pinned SDK history verification passed all 35 entries before this final receipt. Plain strict health failed only because the host-global pm-github extension uses CLI 2026.10.11 while this checkout's host is pinned to 2026.10.4 (extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew). Strict health with synthetic isolated HOME/global tracker and disabled global/system Git config passed; three stale items and one pending telemetry queue entry are advisory. Validation passed with existing linked-path, linked-test-trust and legacy governance advisories. No global extension, telemetry, hosted service or configuration was changed, and no advisory was repaired or suppressed. Version-skew search points to existing certification context pm-csv-3044; this is an environment boundary, not a new package defect. Follow-up pm-csv-bqyu remains open for the separate TypeScript documentation mismatch. All tracked PM writes finish here; regenerate/check changelog and keep exact-head CI receipts in the PR only. Claim remains released; no item closed."
  "2026-10-11T07:49:21.882Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Exact-head DeepScan identified the leftover unused node:fs existsSync import after journal discovery moved to public SDK inventory. Removed only that unused binding; no function or test behavior changes. This is a source cleanup justified by the actual CI finding, rather than a receipt-only rewrite. Prior full npm/Bun/isolated-identity gates passed 275/275 on commit 61f69c6. Validate this cleanup with static checks and the linked behavioral regressions, then require complete CI and packed acceptance on the new exact head. CodeRabbit automatically resolved both original threads after static inspection of the replies; no resolution API or bot mention was used. gh pr edit encountered deprecated projectCards GraphQL, so the preserved body was updated with the authorized structured REST API instead. No new upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-11T07:50:48.307Z",codex-sol-review-150,"Unused-import cleanup validation passed: npm run typecheck, npm run lint and final linked real-journal/Git regressions through pm test --run --only-last --progress (3/3). Release thresholds and executable functions are identical to the three successful full local gates. Full Node 22/26 CI, coverage and packed consumer checks must pass on the new exact head before handoff; those receipts belong in the PR only. Releasing the claim again; no item closed."
  "2026-10-11T07:52:33.642Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator verified the public DeepScan finding and confirms the review worker already removed the unused existsSync binding. Keep one cleanup owner: codex-sol-review-150. Finish static and linked behavioral validation, commit and push this cleanup, then keep the repository source frozen. The orchestrator will run the post-cleanup full isolated npm and Bun gates and verify final CI. Both original threads were resolved automatically by CodeRabbit after replies; the orchestrator will reopen them without posting bot mentions or calling a resolution mutation, preserving the requested open review state."
  "2026-10-11T08:26:08.175Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator final verification: the cleaned source at 852d992 passed both full release gates with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 275 tests, zero failures and skips. Unchanged configured coverage is 100 percent lines, branches and functions across three sources; all three packed consumer scenarios passed, including the minimum supported SDK. The Bun commands exercise the Bun launcher and bunx consumers; Node shebang processes are not native Bun execution. Node 22 and Node 26 CI each passed 275 tests, and CodeQL, Semgrep and DeepScan passed. Both requested review replies were posted; the two review threads were verified open. Source, manifest pins and behavior remain unchanged in this final tracker receipt."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T19:48:35.990Z",codex,"PR 73 Greptile review reconfirmed this open capability gap: aggregate atomic failures can only make a conservative reconciliation claim until prior update state is journaled and restored. pm-csv-5si5 fixes the misleading receipt without pretending this feature is complete."
